 "body": "<style>\n#fig text.tex-i { font-size: 12px; }\n#fig text.tex { font-size: 11px; }\n@media (max-width: 600px) { #fig text.tex-i { font-size: 18px; } #fig text.tex { font-size: 16px; } }\n</style>\n<header class=\"head\"><p class=\"tag\">[example machine, made by Mimir, checked]</p><h1>A DFA for an even number of a's</h1><p class=\"intro\">The alphabet is \\(\\{a, b\\}\\). State \\(q_0\\) means an even number of a's read so far, \\(q_1\\) an odd number. Every state has exactly one move on each symbol, as this course's DFAs must.</p></header>\n<div class=\"board\" style=\"--sticky-fig: 14rem\"><figure><svg id=\"fig\" viewBox=\"0 30 400 160\" role=\"img\"><title>DFA for an even number of a's</title><desc>Two states, q0 and q1. q0 is the start state, entered by an arrow from nowhere, and is accepting, drawn as a double circle. Reading a moves q0 to q1 and q1 to q0. Reading b keeps q0 in q0 and q1 in q1, each by a self-loop on top of the state.</desc>\n<path class=\"mark-swipe\" data-highlight=\"2\" pathLength=\"1\" d=\"M123.6 109.0 Q200.0 30.0 268.8 101.1\"/>\n<path class=\"mark-swipe\" data-highlight=\"3\" pathLength=\"1\" d=\"M289.0 96.4 C276.6 52.4 323.4 52.4 314.0 85.8\"/>\n<path class=\"mark-swipe\" data-highlight=\"4\" pathLength=\"1\" d=\"M276.4 131.0 Q200.0 150.0 134.2 133.6\"/>\n<path class=\"mark-loop\" data-highlight=\"1\" pathLength=\"1\" d=\"M121.6 149.9 C119.7 150.7 113.9 153.2 109.8 154.2 C105.8 155.3 101.6 156.0 97.4 156.3 C93.3 156.5 88.9 156.4 84.8 155.7 C80.7 155.0 76.5 153.8 72.9 152.1 C69.4 150.3 65.9 147.9 63.4 145.1 C60.8 142.4 58.8 139.0 57.5 135.7 C56.2 132.3 55.7 128.6 55.7 125.1 C55.6 121.5 56.3 117.8 57.3 114.3 C58.4 110.8 59.9 107.4 61.9 104.1 C63.8 100.8 66.3 97.5 69.2 94.7 C72.1 91.8 75.6 89.1 79.4 87.0 C83.2 84.9 87.6 83.2 92.0 82.2 C96.3 81.3 101.1 81.0 105.4 81.2 C109.8 81.5 114.2 82.6 118.1 83.9 C122.0 85.3 125.6 87.3 128.9 89.4 C132.1 91.6 135.0 94.2 137.5 97.0 C140.0 99.8 142.2 102.9 143.8 106.2 C145.3 109.5 146.5 113.2 146.